# Generic synthesis of the accelerator with Yosys.
# Run from hw/:   yosys -q synth.ys      (make synth also writes docs/synthesis_yosys.txt)
#
# Two configurations:
#   1. as built   limit/base as register files (every code length reads them
#                 in the same cycle, so no SRAM macro can hold them); the
#                 symbol table as an SRAM with one write port (programming)
#                 and one read port (decode) - the RTL writes symtab in one
#                 always_ff and reads it in another, so it is simple dual-port
#                 as written, and the two are never active in the same phase.
#                 This is the figure the report quotes.
#   2. all-logic  every table flattened into gates and flops.
# Treating every table as a memory macro would look much smaller only because
# `stat` does not count memory cells, so that configuration is not reported.

# ---- 1. as built ------------------------------------------------------------
read_verilog -DSYNTHESIS -sv rtl/bitreader.sv rtl/huffman_decoder.sv rtl/huffman_accel_top.sv
hierarchy -check -top huffman_accel_top
proc; flatten; opt
memory -nomap                       # leave symtab as a memory cell - this is the only
                                    # difference from configuration 2's memory_map.
                                    # limit_r and base_r are already flops by here:
                                    # (* mem2reg *) makes `proc` above do that.
techmap
abc -g AND,NAND,OR,NOR,XOR,XNOR,ANDNOT,ORNOT,MUX   # generic 2-input gates + MUX
opt_clean
tee -o build/stat_asbuilt.txt stat
tee -o build/ltp.txt ltp -noff     # paths stop at flip-flops: the real combinational depth

# ---- 2. every table flattened into logic ------------------------------------
design -reset
read_verilog -DSYNTHESIS -sv rtl/bitreader.sv rtl/huffman_decoder.sv rtl/huffman_accel_top.sv
hierarchy -check -top huffman_accel_top
proc; flatten; opt
memory_map                          # tables become registers + muxes
opt; techmap
abc -g AND,NAND,OR,NOR,XOR,XNOR,ANDNOT,ORNOT,MUX
opt_clean
tee -o build/stat_flat.txt stat
